; err_trace is a git submodule, i.e. a whole upstream repository checked out
; inside this tree - not the two source files we actually build. Its own
; dune files describe a test suite (test/dune, bench/dune) that depends on
; ppx_expect, base, time_now and compiler-libs.
;
; Left visible to dune, those stanzas land in `dune describe` output, and
; tools/asm_audit.ml classifies anything under vendor/ as part of the
; production closure (see its `production_dirs`). base, time_now and
; ppx_expect are all on its `denied` list, so `make asm-purity` fails - and on
; a CI image that does not ship ppx_expect, `dune build @all` fails outright.
;
; `data_only_dirs` is what stops that: dune keeps the files as ordinary
; sources - copy_files# in ../err_trace_local and ../../melange/vendor/err_trace
; still reaches them - but reads no dune file inside, so the submodule
; contributes exactly the one library we declare ourselves and nothing else.
;
; tools/asm-check-planted.sh has a case that deletes this file and requires
; the purity audit to reject the result, so the protection cannot be lost
; silently.

(data_only_dirs err_trace)
